import sys, io
md, hist = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]   # CLAUDE.md, CLAUDE-history.md
s = io.open(md, encoding='utf-8').read()
def R(old, new):
    global s
    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:80]
    s = s.replace(old, new)
R("Pushed up to EC (`754294a`) on 2026-10-31. ED, EE, EF and EG committed, waiting for her push.", "Pushed up to EC (`754294a`) on 2026-10-31. ED, EE, EF, EG and EH committed, waiting for her push.")
R("- Push: ED, EE, EF and EG (four commits), before she opens a cloud window.", "- Push: ED, EE, EF, EG and EH (five commits), before she opens a cloud window.")
R("(sc/wbf45.code.js). |", "(sc/wbf45.code.js). The Grade 1 Workbooks the same way (EH, her 1 Nov 19:44: no plan first, build the best and she checks): 6/8 Time words in twos and threes and counts into notes (ch. 26), the term crossword and build the term (ch. 25), the interval word and both ways (ch. 27), major, then minor (ch. 28), A again, written out (ch. 29); Accidentals and Key Signatures left as they are (sc/wbf46.code.js). |")
R("1. The Workbooks, fun first, floor by floor: the Beginner floor done (EF), the Prelim floor done (EG); next the Grade 1 floor, the same way (her plan first, then one page, then the rest; only the parts better changed).",
  "1. The Workbooks, fun first, floor by floor: the Beginner floor done (EF), the Prelim floor done (EG), the Grade 1 floor done (EH); next the Grade 2 floor, the same way (her 1 Nov 19:44: no plan first; build the best and she checks; only the parts better changed).")
io.open(md, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)
h = io.open(hist, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(h) if l.startswith('| 777 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1 and not any(l.startswith('| 778 |') for l in h)
h[idx[0] + 1:idx[0] + 1] = [
 "| 778 | 2026-11-01 | **The Grade 1 Workbooks, fun first (Build EH; her 19:44 'no, just make it the best you think and keep going: make Grade 1, I'll check').** No plan or page shown first, as she asked. All eight Grade 1 rooms read page by page (Ear Training, Grade 1 has no Workbook). Accidentals and Key Signatures left as they are: set tasks, each page's 'write the names' tied to that step's rule, done alone. In the other five, the parts swapped were the ones that broke the book rules: needing someone else at home, free tasks, the same task again and again; eight swaps and two one-line fixes, none added. Ch. 26 (6/8) p. 2 the week's third row 'while someone claps' → 'while you clap'. P. 5 YOUR TURN 'Listen this week' (someone at home claps) → words in twos and threes: said over and over, a quaver a syllable, the first loud; two syllables loud every second quaver (3/4), three every third (6/8), the room's own groupings; apple done, tiger, pizza, monkey, butterfly, elephant, dinosaur, octopus, four in each bar. P. 6 PLAY 'Write your own' → counts into notes, the other way round from TRY IT: circled counts where notes start (the long-short row: 1 3, 4 5 6, 1 3, 4), draw a crotchet and a quaver, three quavers or a dotted crotchet. Ch. 25 (Terms) p. 2 PLAY 'your teacher plays a scale' → 'set a metronome to each word's number'. P. 5 YOUR TURN, the fifth 'write what it means' in five pages → the term crossword: the room's meanings as clues, a word bank (cantabile, espressivo, leggiero, maestoso, sostenuto), crossings that check the spelling; 9 by 10 squares. P. 6 YOUR TURN 'write the term; make your own' → build the term: twelve tiles, six little words and six terms, each used once (più mosso, meno mosso, con moto, poco a poco cresc. from the room; sempre legato and molto rit. made the room's way); PLAY 'One piece, four ways' with meno mosso in place of 'my own'. Ch. 27 (Intervals) p. 4 YOUR TURN 'Write the note above' (as page 3) → the interval word: the same mix (6th, octave, 7th, 6th) and each note's letter in a box: C A G E. P. 5 PLAY 'your teacher plays six intervals' → both ways: 5 to 8 melodic, then harmonic, as written. Ch. 28 (Chords) p. 3 PLAY 'your teacher plays six triads' → major, then minor: the six from 5 to 10, played as they were and as written minor (numbered 11, not 9 as before). Ch. 29 (Form) p. 5 PLAY 'Your own B' (make one up) → A again, written out: copy bars 1 to 4 after bar 8, the road A B A straight through. Teacher copies: every new answer computed from the same data. Workbooks stay English. Code sc/wbf46.code.js, source sc/patch810.py; test sc/eh811.js (the parts, nothing over in the five Workbooks and Teacher copies, nothing at home needing someone else, the words, the counts, the crossword's runs and squares, the tiles, the word CAGE, the bars of A); the full set. The heads check's 6 known FIX (dots of r 3 or less, not noteheads) are the same since before EF: noted in the handoff. |",
]
io.open(hist, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(h))
print('CLAUDE.md and CLAUDE-history.md updated (row 778)')
